From 8e9fc4b2ae322ae3e547b2383eb58556608fe014 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: briansp2020 <bsp2020@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 01:31:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] moe-cache: widen the decode/verify band to the routed-expert
 MMVQ band (16 on RDNA4)

The expert cache only takes over routed MUL_MAT_ID batches of <= 8 tokens.  With MTP each active
stream verifies n_max+1 tokens per step, so 3+ concurrent streams at n-max 3 (12-16 tokens) fall
to the host path: ids readback + full device synchronize + H2D copy of every used expert, with the
arena unused.  Measured on 2 x R9700 (-sm tensor --n-cpu-moe 48, IQ3_XXS): 2 streams 164 t/s total,
3 streams 46, 4 streams 53 (all-VRAM: 185 / 193 / 201).

The cache serves a batch only through the routed-expert MMVQ kernel (it reads the arena through the
slot remap; MMQ/MMF do not), and the arena redirect already runs before kernel selection, so the band
can follow that kernel's band on the device:

- MOE_EXPERT_CACHE_MAX_TOK becomes moe_cache_max_tok() / moe_cache_max_tok_dev(device): the narrowest
  get_mmvq_mmid_max_batch over the quantized types on the device (16 on RDNA4, CDNA, GCN, RDNA1/2;
  8 on RDNA3 - where the 16-wide MoE MMVQ band is off because it is incorrect on gfx1100 - and on
  NVIDIA), never below the historical 8.  GGML_MOE_CACHE_MAX_TOK lowers it (8 = the old band).
- New backend iface hook moe_cache_band: the CUDA backend reports its device's band, the meta backend
  the narrowest over its devices; the scheduler's four literal 8s (take-over before the ids readback,
  per-layer split grouping, decode-band rebalance, device-gather gate) ask the backend instead.
  A backend without the hook keeps 8; the meta backend's moe_cache_update follows its band too.
  CPU / RPC get explicit NULL entries.
- The device-side admission policy kernel stages a pass's admitted experts in a fixed shared-memory
  list (MOE_CACHE_POLICY_MAX_FILL, was 64): past it, an expert was still marked resident but its fill
  was never staged, so the next pass read a stale arena slot.  The list is now 256 (16 tokens x 16
  experts) and the loop stops admitting when it is full (the expert stays cold, served from the host
  alias).  64 was already below n_used * 8 = 80 for a 10-expert model at the old band.

Same 2 x R9700 setup with the band at 16: 3 streams 175 t/s total, 4 streams 191; 1-2 streams
unchanged; greedy output equals the all-VRAM output (the 9-16 token prompt now takes the same MoE
MMVQ kernel), plain == MTP; 0 faults.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
